{{ intro }}

Pool-based Active Learning
--------------------------

The strategy chooses which samples to label from an available pool.
The groups below show different prediction tasks and annotation settings.

.. _pool-based-active-learning-classification:

Single-output Classification
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Each sample has one class label. The animations show the classifier's
decision boundary, labeled samples, and the query strategy's utility scores.

.. image:: /examples/pool_classification_legend.png
   :alt: Legend for class labels, decision boundaries, labeled samples, and utility scores.

{{ gallery("pool-classification") }}

Multi-label Classification
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

A sample can have several labels. Each animation shows one panel per label.
Querying a sample reveals its complete label vector. The panels share the
same acquisition utility, while each has its own decision boundary.
The legend below applies separately to each panel: class 0 and class 1 mean
that the panel's label is absent or present, respectively. Gray markers
identify samples whose label vectors have been acquired.

.. image:: /examples/pool_classification_legend.png
   :alt: Legend applied per label: binary label values, decision boundaries, acquired samples, and utility scores.

{{ gallery("pool-multilabel") }}

.. _pool-based-active-learning-regression:

Regression
~~~~~~~~~~

Each sample has a continuous target value. The animations show the fitted
regression curve, labeled samples, and acquisition utilities. Some examples
select several samples per cycle.

.. image:: /examples/pool_regression_legend.png
   :alt: Legend for the regression curve, utility scores, and labeled and unlabeled samples.

{{ gallery("pool-regression") }}

.. _pool-based-active-learning-multi-annotator-learning:

Classification with Multiple Annotators
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Several annotators can provide a class label for a sample. These examples
show how a strategy selects sample–annotator pairs when annotator reliability
varies.

.. image:: /examples/pool_multi_annotator_legend.png
   :alt: Legend for class labels, annotator correctness, decision boundaries, and utility scores.

{{ gallery("pool-multi-annotator") }}

.. _stream-based-active-learning-classification:

Stream-based Active Learning
----------------------------

Samples arrive in sequence, and the strategy decides which ones to label
within its budget. The current animations demonstrate single-output
classification, showing arriving samples and the evolving decision boundary.

.. image:: /examples/stream_classification_legend.png
   :alt: Legend for class labels, unlabeled and current samples, and the decision boundary.

{{ gallery("stream-classification") }}

